# deploy/.gitignore — secret-hygiene safety net for the whole deploy/
# tree (gitops manifests, terraform, runbooks). PR-K0, §K (#54).
#
# Nothing secret is EVER committed under deploy/. Application secrets
# flow through the External Secrets Operator + Vault — see
# deploy/gitops/secrets/README.md. This file is the belt-and-suspenders
# backstop for an accidental `git add`; the gitleaks pre-commit hook
# (.pre-commit-config.yaml at the repo root) is the other layer.

# --- Private key / certificate material -------------------------------
# Public certs (*.crt, CA bundles) are NOT ignored — cert-manager and
# CA bundles are fine to track. Only private material is blocked here.
*.pem
*.key
*.der
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore

# --- SSH private keys (frequently extensionless, so name-matched) ------
id_rsa
id_dsa
id_ecdsa
id_ed25519
*_rsa
*_dsa
*_ecdsa
*_ed25519
*.ppk
deploy-key
*-deploy-key

# --- Raw Kubernetes Secret manifests ----------------------------------
# Plaintext `kind: Secret` files must never exist (External Secrets
# only). Both `.yaml` and `.yml` spellings are blocked. The `!` lines
# keep *ExternalSecret* CRs trackable — those carry Vault key
# *references*, never secret values. Name ExternalSecret files
# `*-external-secret.yaml` (see deploy/gitops/secrets/README.md).
*-secret.yaml
*-secret.yml
*.secret.yaml
*.secret.yml
secret.yaml
secret.yml
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml
# `!*external-secret.{yaml,yml}` already covers the hyphenated
# `*-external-secret.*`; `!*externalsecret.{yaml,yml}` covers the
# un-hyphenated spelling. These negations are sufficient.
!*external-secret.yaml
!*external-secret.yml
!*externalsecret.yaml
!*externalsecret.yml
# Exception (PR-K4): `registry-secret.yaml` is a Helm *template* inside
# the vendored local-path-provisioner chart, not a plaintext Secret — it
# renders nothing unless a private registry is configured (it is not).
# Keeping it tracked preserves the chart's byte-for-byte upstream
# provenance (see addons/local-path-provisioner/PROVENANCE.md).
!gitops/addons/local-path-provisioner/charts/local-path-provisioner/templates/registry-secret.yaml

# --- Kubeconfigs / cluster credentials --------------------------------
kubeconfig*
*.kubeconfig
*-kubeconfig

# --- Environment files ------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.env

# --- Terraform state + vars (PR-K1) -----------------------------------
# tfstate embeds resolved values (incl. secrets) in plaintext; never
# commit it. `.terraform.lock.hcl` IS committed (provider version pins)
# so it is deliberately absent below.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform/
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example

# --- Helm values deliberately holding secret values -------------------
# Secret values must NOT go in a values file at all (External Secrets
# only). These two explicit names are a backstop for a file created
# under that deliberate naming — kept narrow on purpose: a broad
# `*secret*` glob would also swallow a legitimate, non-secret values
# file such as `external-secrets.values.yaml` (the ESO addon's values).
secret-values.yaml
secret-values.yml
*-secret-values.yaml
*-secret-values.yml
